    {
      "duration_ms": 10500,
      "caption": "Sections are named, typed units: .text, .rodata, .data, .bss, .symtab.",
      "narration": "Sections are what the compiler emits and the linker merges. Each has a name, type, flags and size, like .text for code or .rodata for constants.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Sections: linker's units",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 6,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "secs",
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            ".text  SHT_PROGBITS  AX",
            ".rodata  SHT_PROGBITS  A",
            ".data  SHT_PROGBITS  WA",
            ".bss  SHT_NOBITS  WA",
            ".symtab  SHT_SYMTAB"
          ],
          "x": 8,
          "y": 20.0,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 600,
          "enter": "slide-up",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "id": "hl-secs",
          "type": "highlight",
          "target": "secs",
          "at": 2300
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "caption": "Segments are runtime memory ranges: permissions, file offset, vaddr.",
      "narration": "Segments describe what to mmap. Each PT_LOAD entry gives an offset, a virtual address, sizes and permissions. The kernel never reads section headers.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Segments: loader's units",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 6,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "ph",
